# PLAN — Whole-GPU passthrough for selected Proxmox VMs

> Earlier approved scope retained for traceability. `master.plan` records the
> implemented runner/playbook architecture and any deliberate scope changes.

## Summary

- Keep 0.0.5 unchanged on current main at bd5bbc3; GPU work is post-0.0.5 and must not merge before
  that tag.

- After human approval, save this plan as /Users/x/Desktop/devs.guide/prompts/proxmox/vm/
  gpu.passthrough.plan.md, preserving all existing prompt-workspace changes.

- Create and switch to feature/vm/gpu from exact current main. Stop if origin/main changes before
  branch creation.

- Support whole, node-local GPU passthrough to QEMU VMs on PVE 6.4 and 9.x. Docker/LLM workloads use a
  Linux VM; direct host/LXC GPU exposure is excluded.

- Treat the five WX 4100 pairs as test fixtures only. Discovery remains vendor-neutral and address-
  based.

## Operator workflow

Provide one published runner with:

setup/vm/gpu.sh --action inventory|preflight|prepare|verify|attach|detach|status|unprepare

Stable flags:

--vm VMID
--gpu FULL_PCI_BDF
--profile macos-desktop|windows-desktop|linux-desktop|linux-compute
--hostpci-index auto|N
--output human|json
--dry-run
--yes
--start
--allow-host-display-loss

- Live platform facts always select the release adapter. `--release` is an
  optional assertion and never an override.

- `--gpu` has no default and must identify a display function, not only a
  physical slot. Every targeted action first inventories all GPU slots and
  functions, matches the supplied BDF, and passes complete inventory plus the
  explicit selection to Ansible.

- Missing VM/GPU/profile values open readable interactive selectors only when a TTY exists;
  noninteractive runs require explicit flags.

- inventory discovers every GPU from machine-readable PCI/sysfs data, groups
  every function belonging to one physical slot, and reports BDF, class,
  vendor/device/subsystem IDs, driver, IOMMU group, boot-VGA status, NUMA node,
  VM assignment, and reset capability.

- preflight requires a local, stopped, non-HA QEMU VM; validates Q35/guest-profile requirements, IOMMU
  isolation, complete multifunction selection, and absence of conflicting assignments.

- prepare enables CPU-appropriate IOMMU configuration, loads VFIO modules, and persistently reserves
  only the selected full PCI addresses. It never binds by shared vendor/device IDs or globally
  blacklists AMD/NVIDIA drivers.

- Host preparation writes exact-BDF driver_override handling into initramfs, refreshes GRUB or Proxmox
  boot tooling appropriately, records rollback state, and reports that a reboot is required. It never
  reboots automatically.

- verify runs after reboot and proves that only the selected GPU functions use vfio-pci; identical
  unselected GPUs must retain their previous drivers.

- attach allocates the lowest free hostpciN unless explicitly selected, preserves existing PCI
  devices, records the original VM display configuration, and leaves the VM stopped unless --start is
  supplied.

- Desktop profiles use the passed-through GPU as primary (x-vga) and disable virtual VGA after
  explicit console-loss confirmation. linux-compute passes the complete GPU while retaining the
  virtual console.

- detach removes only the feature-owned PCI entry and restores the exact previous display
  configuration.

- unprepare requires the GPU to be detached and unused, restores managed host configuration, rebuilds
  boot artifacts, and requires another explicit reboot.

- Serialize mutations with a lock and persist non-secret ownership/rollback state under /etc/ansible/
  proxmox/.

## Safety and compatibility

- Normalize function-qualified addresses such as `18:00.0` to
  `0000:18:00.0`; reject slot-only input and select all inventory-backed
  functions from the matched slot, including audio or USB functions.

- Refuse mixed IOMMU groups, running VMs, existing assignments, HA-managed VMs, migration while
  attached, occupied hostpciN entries, stale ownership state, or non-Q35 guests.

- Refuse a boot/host-console GPU unless --allow-host-display-loss --yes is supplied and out-of-band
  access is acknowledged.

- Do not add ACS overrides, ROM patches, SR-IOV, mediated/vGPU support, iGPU support, vendor driver
  installation, guest driver installation, or automatic reset workarounds.

- Record reset limitations clearly; a GPU that wedges after guest shutdown may require a host power
  cycle.

- Use raw node-local BDFs on both supported PVE versions; modern resource mappings are deferred.
- Follow the PVE 6.4 and current PCI passthrough/bootloader contracts documented in the PVE 6.4 guide
  (https://pve.proxmox.com/pve-docs-6/pve-admin-guide.pdf) and current PVE guide
  (https://pve.proxmox.com/pve-docs/pve-admin-guide.pdf).

## Publication and validation

- Publish the runner and declared dependencies through the existing Pages artifact workflow; PR
  validation must not deploy.

- Add a dedicated GPU contract validator covering shell syntax, interface stability, publication
  wiring, dry-run behavior, state ownership, and rollback.

- CI fixtures include identical GPU IDs and prove an explicitly selected BDF
  never captures another physical slot.

- Cover missing audio functions, extra multifunction devices, mixed IOMMU groups, boot GPUs, absent
  IOMMU, duplicate IDs, running/HA VMs, occupied PCI slots, stale manifests, and PVE 6.4/9.x command
  differences.

- Remote acceptance requires rollback-capable PVE 6.4 and 9.x nodes: inventory, dry-run, preparation,
  reboot verification, attach, guest detection, restart/reset test, detach, unprepare, reboot, and
  proof that host drivers/configuration were restored.

- Test at least one desktop profile and linux-compute; untested guest/vendor combinations remain
  explicitly labeled untested.

## Release and persistence assumptions

- The official 0.0.5 tag remains based on main, not the checked-out GPU branch.
- GPU commits do not modify the 0.0.5 release plan or enter its tag.
- Saving the approved plan adds only the new plan file; existing dirty prompt-repository files are
  neither staged nor changed.
